      "title": "Australia news live: Duniam promises ‘humdinger’ immigration policy and urges Coalition not to ‘act like a government in exile’",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/sep/06/australia-news-live-albanese-labor-party-coaltion-liberal-party-nepal-floods-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>Follow today’s news live</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p><strong>Duniam targets ‘frivolous’ asylum seeker claims</strong></p><p>The opposition is “very close” to “having a full migration package”, Duniam says. He says they’re willing to work with the government and that illegal overstayers must be deported.</p><p>We spend more per student per year than we ever have before and we’ve got declining standards across the board, and the problem with the curriculum is we have left foundations behind.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/sep/06/australia-news-live-albanese-labor-party-coaltion-liberal-party-nepal-floods-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
